ZX Spectrum 48K quick start
===========================

1. Start the `ZX Spectrum 48K` virtual computer.
2. In the Byte Memory settings, load a 16 KiB Spectrum ROM at address 0000H.
3. Open one of the assembly examples in the editor and compile it with AS-Z80.
   The examples use `org 8000H`, so compilation writes them at address 32768.
4. From Spectrum BASIC run `RANDOMIZE USR 32768`.

The Z80 CPU status panel can also load a stopped 48K machine snapshot. Use
`Load snapshot...` for `.sna` or `.z80` files. Z80 v1, v2, and v3 48K files are
accepted; 128K and banked snapshots are rejected because this computer model has
no compatible paging hardware.

ROM and tape files can be found at:

- https://www.planetemu.net/roms/sinclair-zx-spectrum-z80
- https://worldofspectrum.org/
- https://wowroms.com/en/roms/list/zx+spectrum
- https://mdfs.net/Software/Spectrum/ROMImages/

Example sources:

- `border_stripes.asm` beginner example: set the border, bitmap, and attributes.
- `zx_audio.asm` standalone ZX Spectrum ROM `BEEP` melody demo (assemble for 32768 / 8000H, then run with `RANDOMIZE USR 32768`).
- `twinkle_beeper.asm` (assemble for 32768 / 8000H, then run with `RANDOMIZE USR 32768`)
- `ay_ode_to_joy.asm` AY-3-8910 three-voice demo. Add the AY device to the computer first, then assemble for 32768 / 8000H and run with `RANDOMIZE USR 32768`.

AS-Z80 tutorial
---------------

Numbers can use hexadecimal suffix `H` (`8000H`), decimal notation, or symbols
declared with `equ`. Labels end with `:` and can be used by jumps, calls, and
data directives. `db` emits bytes and `dw` emits little-endian words.

The screen bitmap starts at `4000H`; its attributes start at `5800H`. Port
`FEH` controls the border and beeper. Begin with `border_stripes.asm`, then use
`twinkle_beeper.asm` to see subroutines, a data table, and port output.
